1
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:39,289
My name is Richard.

2
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,543
So what else do you need to know?

3
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:46,171
Stuff about my family or where l'm from?

4
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:48,923
None of that matters.

5
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:53,887
Not once you cross the ocean
and cut yourself loose,...

6
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:58,141
..looking for something more beautiful,
something more exciting,...

7
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:01,269
..and yes, l admit,
something more dangerous.

8
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:05,482
So after 18 hours in the back of an airplane,...

9
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:10,153
..three dumb movies, two plastic meals,
six beers and absolutely no sleep,...

10
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:12,197
..l finally touch down...

11
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,783
- Hey, you! How about you?
- ..in Bangkok.

12
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:17,702
Do you want to go to the waterfall?
Floating market!

13
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:19,913
1,500. Cheap for you! Come on! Hey!

14
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:22,582
Hey! Do you need somewhere to stay?

15
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:25,543
- l'll find my own place, thanks.
- What you want, man?

16
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:27,962
And this is it. Bangkok.

17
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:30,131
Good-time city.

18
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:32,300
Gateway to Southeast Asia.

19
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:37,263
Where dollars and Deutschmarks get turned
into counter feit watches and genuine scars.

20
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:39,849
Good time! Boy! Girl! Fucking!
No problem!

21
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:43,978
- This is where the hungry come to feed.
- You wanna drink snake blood?

22
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:47,023
Wait a minute. Did you say snake blood?

23
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:49,192
Oh, yeah!

24
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:52,779
- No, thanks.
- What is wrong with snake blood?

25
00:01:52,862 --> 00:01:56,866
- l just... don't like the idea.
- Maybe you're scared.

26
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,786
- Afraid of something new.
- l just don't like the idea.

27
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:01,746
Like every tourist!

28
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,915
You want it all be safe.

29
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,084
Just like America!

30
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:11,047
So never refuse an invitation.

31
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:15,802
Never resist the unfamiliar.

32
00:02:31,526 --> 00:02:33,611
Never fail to be polite.

33
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:35,655
Gentlemen,...

34
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:37,824
..that was excellent.

35
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:39,993
And never outstay your welcome.

36
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:45,165
Just keep your mind open
and suck in the experience.

37
00:02:46,041 --> 00:02:48,126
And if it hurts,...

38
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:50,295
..it's probably worth it.

39
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:53,214
Hey.

40
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:55,383
- Good evening.
- Hi.

41
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:57,719
- Can l get a room, please?
- Yes.

42
00:03:04,476 --> 00:03:06,561
(TV)

43
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:17,864
The only downer is,
everyone's got the same idea.

44
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:20,075
We all travel thousands ofmiles...

45
00:03:20,158 --> 00:03:24,371
..just to watch TVand check into somewhere
with all the comforts of home.

46
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:27,540
And you gotta ask yourself,...

47
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:31,544
We'll have this place cleaned up
in a jiffy, so don't you worry!

48
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,713
..what is the point of that?

49
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,841
(TV: bombs exploding)

50
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:06,413
(drops wash bag)

51
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:09,958
(Richard nervously clears his throat)

52
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:15,964
- Et voilá!
- Thank you.

53
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,341
Bonsoir.

54
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,052
Bonsoir.

55
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,847
Good night.

56
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:27,058
And as for travelling alone,...

57
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:28,935
..fuck it!

58
00:04:29,019 --> 00:04:32,605
lf that's the way it has to be,
then that's the way it is.

59
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:45,702
(rhythmic bumping)

60
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:51,499
(man and woman groaning with pleasure)

61
00:04:57,339 --> 00:05:00,633
(Scottish accent) Everybody happy?!

62
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:05,096
Everybody having a good time, eh?

63
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:07,265
Fuck you! Fuck you!

64
00:05:07,349 --> 00:05:09,434
(woman) Please shut up, OK?

65
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:11,603
(man) Bastard parasites!

66
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:13,271
Viruses!

67
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,191
That's fuckin' great! Cancers!

68
00:05:16,274 --> 00:05:18,360
Bastard cancers!

69
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:21,946
(martial arts cry)

70
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:25,992
(man) Hé! Tu vas fermer ta putain de gueule?!

71
00:05:26,076 --> 00:05:30,789
(man) A big, chunky Charlie
that's eat in' up the whole fuckin' world!

72
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:36,961
- (bang)
- Hey!

73
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:39,547
(knocking) Hey, you!

74
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:48,390
- You got anything to smoke?
- No, l don't have anything to smoke!

75
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,560
That's nae problem, pal, cos, er...

76
00:05:52,644 --> 00:05:55,689
(sniffs) ..l've got loads of the fuckin' stuff.

77
00:05:56,147 --> 00:05:58,233
- (thud)
- (man grunts)

78
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,694
(bottles clink)

79
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,374
Do ya understand what l'm say in'?

80
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,042
Yeah.

81
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:18,420
No, you don't.

82
00:06:20,005 --> 00:06:22,215
No, you're right. l don't.

83
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:27,303
(loudly) Ahh, that's better!

84
00:06:31,725 --> 00:06:33,810
(softly) Thanks.

85
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:37,063
lt was the beach. You understand?

86
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:41,276
The beach. lt was too...

87
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:46,990
..beautiful. Too much input, too much...
sensation. l-l try to keep it under control,...

88
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:51,244
..but it just keeps spilling out
and spilling out and spilling out.

89
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:55,165
You see, erm...

90
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:57,334
..she's on an island.

91
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:01,588
And the island is... is perfect.

92
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:04,883
l mean... l mean, real perfection here.

93
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:08,428
l'm not just talking about... "Oh, that's nice."

94
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:12,057
lt's the real fuckin' deal, OK?

95
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:16,311
lt's perfect.

96
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:19,230
See, it's like a... a lagoon.

97
00:07:19,314 --> 00:07:21,399
Ya know, a tidal... lagoon.

98
00:07:21,483 --> 00:07:23,568
See, it's sealed in by cliffs.

99
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:26,613
Totally fuckin' secret, totally fuckin'...

100
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:28,782
..forbidden.

101
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,825
And nobody can ever, ever,...

102
00:07:30,909 --> 00:07:32,994
..ever, ever go there. Ever.

103
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:36,790
But a few people went,...

104
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:39,125
..once upon a time.

105
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:42,295
Men and women with ideals.
You understand?

106
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:46,758
l'm not just talking about the usual...
travellin' fuckin' wanks.

107
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:49,928
Do you believe in that place?

108
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:52,889
No.

109
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:56,393
But l guess you're gonna tell me
that l should, right?

110
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:04,693
lt doesnae fuckin' matter
what l think any more.

111
00:08:04,776 --> 00:08:06,861
lt's up to you.

112
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:10,490
ldeals, eh?

113
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:12,784
We were just fuckin' parasites!

114
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:15,370
The big, chunky Charlie!

115
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:22,335
See, l-l was the one...

116
00:08:22,419 --> 00:08:26,423
..that was trying to find the cure.
Procurer of the cure.

117
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,260
l said to them "You've got to leave."

118
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:33,763
"You've got to leave this place."

119
00:08:35,432 --> 00:08:37,642
But they would nae listen.

120
00:08:41,604 --> 00:08:44,399
No offence an' all, but...

121
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:48,153
..you're fucked in the head, right?

122
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,454
(both snigger)

123
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:04,502
Here, Richard.

124
00:09:08,006 --> 00:09:10,091
lt's been nice know in' you, man.

125
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:14,095
Yeah. You, too.

126
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:20,143
(thud)

127
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:38,578
(electricity crackles)

128
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:42,999
Be careful! Electric... Electricity!

129
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:48,213
- Ma'am! Ma'am! (makes buzzing sound)
- Chill, man!

130
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:50,423
No worry!

131
00:09:50,507 --> 00:09:52,592
(electricity crackles)

132
00:09:57,806 --> 00:09:59,599
Hey! Man.

133
00:09:59,683 --> 00:10:01,768
There is a letter for you.

134
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:03,728
A what?

135
00:10:03,812 --> 00:10:05,689
Letter on your door.

136
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,006
No fuckin' way!

137
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:35,218
Do you...

138
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:54,195
- Hello?
- (knocks on door)

139
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,565
You hope...

140
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:33,151
..and you dream,...

141
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:38,156
..but you neverbelieve that
something's gonna happen foryou.

142
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:41,826
Not like it does in the movies.

143
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:47,123
And when it actually does,...

144
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,086
..you want it to feel different.

145
00:11:53,797 --> 00:11:56,299
More visceral.

146
00:11:56,383 --> 00:11:58,843
More real.

147
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:08,895
l was waiting for it to hit me.

148
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,526
But it just wouldn't happen.

149
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:17,404
(man) The name ofMr Daffy Duck.

150
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:19,572
Birthplace: Never Never Land.

151
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:21,741
Gonna fuck up all the paperwork.

152
00:12:22,409 --> 00:12:27,664
The police were pissed because he was
travelling under a false passport.

153
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:29,833
Go ahead, sign the statement.

154
00:12:38,133 --> 00:12:40,135
lt's OK.

155
00:12:40,218 --> 00:12:44,514
lt just say he cut his wrists -
already dead when you found him.

156
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:48,893
But they didn't ask me about the map, so...

157
00:12:48,977 --> 00:12:50,562
No problem.

158
00:12:50,645 --> 00:12:53,648
..l didn't tell 'em.

159
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,696
You have a nice day.

160
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:08,079
Good luck!

161
00:13:08,163 --> 00:13:10,248
Excuse me.

162
00:13:14,878 --> 00:13:16,963
Look... l mean,...

163
00:13:18,548 --> 00:13:21,259
..this island may not actually even exist.

164
00:13:21,343 --> 00:13:24,095
Even if it does, l don't know
if we can get there or not.

165
00:13:24,179 --> 00:13:27,057
l just wondered if you wanted
to come with me.

166
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:29,225
That's all.

167
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:31,394
(** "Woozy" by Faithless)

168
00:13:33,313 --> 00:13:35,398
(nervous sigh)

169
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:44,324
Hey! You wanna take a hike?

170
00:13:45,116 --> 00:13:47,202
Uh... a-a trip, ajourney?

171
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:49,913
With y-your girlfriend and me?

172
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:52,290
l mean, the two of you and me. Together.

173
00:13:52,374 --> 00:13:54,959
- l-l'm talking about the secret isla-...
- Hi.

174
00:13:55,043 --> 00:13:56,378
Hi.

175
00:14:00,298 --> 00:14:04,094
l just feel like everyone tries
to do something different, but...

176
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:06,596
..you always wind up doing the same thing.

177
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:14,521
l realised that l had absolutely no idea
of how l was gonna get there.

178
00:14:16,731 --> 00:14:18,358
But Étienne...

179
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:21,945
l mean, l have to hand it
to the guy. He was great.

180
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:24,739
l mean, he organised
the whole thing - tickets,...

181
00:14:24,823 --> 00:14:27,158
..timetables, the whole damn trip.

182
00:14:27,242 --> 00:14:31,371
Bangkok to Surat Thani.
Surat Thani to Na Thon.

183
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:33,540
Na Thon to Chaweng.

184
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,959
500 miles in 24 hours,...

185
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:38,545
..at less than 400 baht.

186
00:14:39,379 --> 00:14:41,715
Trust me, that's a very good deal.

187
00:14:47,053 --> 00:14:49,472
We were headed for the great unknown.

188
00:14:49,556 --> 00:14:53,643
But to get there, we had to follow
the regular tourist trail.

189
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:12,787
** A little less pushin'
and shovin'

190
00:15:12,871 --> 00:15:13,872
** Take it easy

191
00:15:13,955 --> 00:15:16,291
** You could even getsleazy

192
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:18,209
** Come around

193
00:15:18,293 --> 00:15:20,045
** Watch a movie

194
00:15:20,128 --> 00:15:21,713
** With the sound down

195
00:15:21,796 --> 00:15:23,882
** And get woozy...

196
00:15:23,965 --> 00:15:27,677
lt's arranged. Tomorrow morning. 1800 baht.

197
00:15:27,761 --> 00:15:29,637
Ah, great man! Nice work!

198
00:15:29,721 --> 00:15:32,724
There is one problem.
He will not take us to the island.

199
00:15:32,807 --> 00:15:36,436
lt's in the national park
and it's forbidden to go there. But...

200
00:15:37,187 --> 00:15:40,565
..we are allowed to travel to this one
to stay for one night.

201
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,859
Yeah... No, see, that's the wrong one.

202
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:45,028
Yeah, l know that.

203
00:15:45,111 --> 00:15:47,447
Right. But how do we get
from there to there?

204
00:15:47,530 --> 00:15:50,325
- We swim.
- We swim?

205
00:15:50,408 --> 00:15:54,037
Yeah. We leave our rucksacks
on this island and then we swim.

206
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:58,249
- You can swim, can't you, Richard?
- Of course l can swim.

207
00:15:58,333 --> 00:16:01,795
- So no problem.
- So h-how far is it, though?

208
00:16:01,878 --> 00:16:04,047
l don't know. One or two kilometres.

209
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:08,259
- Cool. Cool... Not far at all(!)
- Stop it, Richard. lt will be worth it.

210
00:16:08,343 --> 00:16:11,346
An adventure. And just... the three of us.

211
00:16:15,767 --> 00:16:17,977
(thunderclap)

212
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:20,772
Uh-oh.

213
00:16:22,273 --> 00:16:24,776
(mocks Étienne's accent) "Can you swim?"

214
00:16:24,859 --> 00:16:29,656
"l can swim! Oh, yeah! l am French and
l have the beautiful girlfriend, too! Huh!"

215
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:34,703
Great(!)

216
00:16:34,786 --> 00:16:37,372
- God dammit!
- (man) Locked out, huh?

217
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:41,084
Yeah.

218
00:16:42,544 --> 00:16:44,629
- (youth) Lost your key?
- Uh-huh.

219
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:48,258
- (man) Bummer!
- Yeah, bummer!

220
00:16:49,843 --> 00:16:53,221
So, uh... you wanna
grab a beer or somethin'?

221
00:16:55,807 --> 00:16:57,892
(thunderclap)

222
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:03,898
- You're better off without her.
- Sammy, how the fuck would you know?!

223
00:17:03,982 --> 00:17:06,067
You've never even met her!

224
00:17:06,151 --> 00:17:09,654
l'm just tryin' to help the guy
through the dark times.

225
00:17:09,738 --> 00:17:12,449
- lt's not a problem.
- You see, Zeph?

226
00:17:12,532 --> 00:17:15,827
- lt's not a problem.
- Change the fuckin' subject.

227
00:17:16,745 --> 00:17:21,416
All right. Let's talk about how you spend
an hour in front of the mirror every day.

228
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:25,837
Oh, that's nice(!) You know this guy?
He likes to wipe his ass with tree leaves.

229
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:29,341
He thinks he's some sort of
jungle commando.

230
00:17:29,424 --> 00:17:31,176
- Whatever.
- (Zeph) l swear to God!

231
00:17:31,259 --> 00:17:33,345
- (Sammy) Whatever.
- Damn!

232
00:17:33,428 --> 00:17:35,305
l presume...

233
00:17:35,388 --> 00:17:38,558
..you know the story
of the Kentucky fried mouse.

234
00:17:38,641 --> 00:17:40,352
Yeah.

235
00:17:40,435 --> 00:17:42,520
Woman bites into a chicken leg...

236
00:17:42,604 --> 00:17:44,939
..and it turns out to be, uh... a mouse.

237
00:17:45,023 --> 00:17:46,358
Right?

238
00:17:46,441 --> 00:17:48,526
lt's an urban myth.

239
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:53,948
Exactly. lt always happened
to a friend of a friend of someone else.

240
00:17:54,032 --> 00:17:55,825
- So?
- So,...

241
00:17:55,909 --> 00:18:00,288
..l guess there's this urban myth
goin' around here at the moment.

242
00:18:00,372 --> 00:18:02,082
lt's about a beach.

243
00:18:03,792 --> 00:18:05,877
- Yeah?
- Uh-huh.

244
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:09,381
And this beach is... perfect, man.

245
00:18:09,464 --> 00:18:11,549
lt's on an island, right?

246
00:18:12,050 --> 00:18:14,302
Hidden from the sea.

247
00:18:15,053 --> 00:18:17,138
Now, imagine. You got...

248
00:18:17,222 --> 00:18:18,848
..pure white sand.

249
00:18:18,932 --> 00:18:21,017
Crystal-clear water.

250
00:18:21,101 --> 00:18:24,187
- Palm trees.
- (Sammy) Yeah, with coconuts and shit!

251
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:26,648
Yo, tell him the best part, dawg.

252
00:18:26,731 --> 00:18:27,774
Plus...

253
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:29,943
..enough dope, Richard,...

254
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:32,779
..to smoke all day, every day...

255
00:18:32,862 --> 00:18:36,157
- ..for the rest of your goddamn life!
- Yeah! Mad weed!

256
00:18:38,201 --> 00:18:43,832
(Zeph) Only a few people know exactly where
it is, and they keep it absolutely secret.

257
00:18:43,915 --> 00:18:46,960
No one's actually ever met
any of these people.

258
00:18:47,043 --> 00:18:49,546
Exactly. lt's a Kentucky fried mouse!

259
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:50,672
Hm!

260
00:18:50,755 --> 00:18:53,550
Although, if l had a key to a place like that,...

261
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:59,180
..l'd keep it to myself cos... you don't want
every fuckin' asshole in Thailand...

262
00:18:59,264 --> 00:19:01,057
..turnin' up! Boo-boo!

263
00:19:01,141 --> 00:19:03,393
(Sammy) Yeah, yeah.

264
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:06,062
So whaddaya think
about that story, Richard?

265
00:19:09,399 --> 00:19:11,234
lt's good.

266
00:19:11,317 --> 00:19:13,403
lt's a good story.

267
00:19:13,486 --> 00:19:16,156
Hey, you! l got your key!

268
00:19:18,867 --> 00:19:21,494
Now, l know it wasn't a part of the plan,...

269
00:19:21,578 --> 00:19:24,706
..but l made a decision
to leave a copy of the map.

270
00:19:25,498 --> 00:19:28,918
l'm not gonna say it was
the best decision l ever made.

271
00:19:29,919 --> 00:19:34,466
l told myself that spreading news
is a part of a traveller's nature.

272
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:38,011
But if l was being completely honest,...

273
00:19:39,095 --> 00:19:41,264
..l was just like everybody else:

274
00:19:42,098 --> 00:19:44,517
..shit-scared of the great unknown.

275
00:19:45,268 --> 00:19:48,396
Desperate to take
a little piece of home with me.

276
00:20:01,034 --> 00:20:04,162
- (Étienne) Richard?
- Are you ready?

277
00:20:04,245 --> 00:20:06,331
Yeah, yeah. l'm coming.

278
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,585
Let's go.

279
00:20:10,669 --> 00:20:12,962
(** "8 Ball" by Underworld)

280
00:20:53,294 --> 00:20:55,380
** Feel dead

281
00:20:55,672 --> 00:20:57,507
** Feel dead

282
00:20:58,049 --> 00:20:59,759
** Feel dead

283
00:21:00,135 --> 00:21:02,429
** Feel dead

284
00:21:02,512 --> 00:21:05,640
** Happy

285
00:21:10,103 --> 00:21:11,563
Francoise?

286
00:21:11,646 --> 00:21:14,274
Chut! Étienne will be angry if l wake him.

287
00:21:14,357 --> 00:21:17,736
He thinks l waste time,
taking photographs of the sky.

288
00:21:19,654 --> 00:21:21,740
Oh...

289
00:21:23,408 --> 00:21:25,035
(shutter clicks)

290
00:21:27,495 --> 00:21:30,623
- l think so, too.
- Yeah?

291
00:21:30,707 --> 00:21:32,792
Have a look.

292
00:21:35,128 --> 00:21:38,089
One night, l will get the perfect photograph.

293
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:49,934
Hi!

294
00:21:50,018 --> 00:21:52,103
Whoa!

295
00:22:05,325 --> 00:22:07,410
You realise that,...

296
00:22:07,494 --> 00:22:09,579
..in the eternity of space,...

297
00:22:11,706 --> 00:22:14,959
..there's probably a planet out there, right,...

298
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:17,545
..just like this one,...

299
00:22:17,629 --> 00:22:19,381
..where another you...

300
00:22:19,464 --> 00:22:22,175
..is photographing back down towards us.

301
00:22:23,134 --> 00:22:27,681
l mean, essentially, you are photographing
yourself in a parallel universe.

302
00:22:27,764 --> 00:22:29,849
lncredible.

303
00:22:31,017 --> 00:22:33,103
Yeah...

304
00:22:33,186 --> 00:22:35,772
There are infinite worlds out there, ya know?

305
00:22:35,855 --> 00:22:38,274
Where anything you want to happen...

306
00:22:38,358 --> 00:22:40,068
..does happen.

307
00:22:40,151 --> 00:22:42,237
Richard, do you know something?

308
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:43,321
Hm?

309
00:22:43,405 --> 00:22:46,324
This is just the kind of pretentious bullshit...

310
00:22:46,408 --> 00:22:50,328
..Americans always say to French girls...
so they can sleep with them.

311
00:22:53,373 --> 00:22:55,458
God! Sorry.

312
00:22:55,542 --> 00:22:57,711
l thought l was doin' pretty good.

313
00:22:57,794 --> 00:23:00,296
lt's just the sky, Richard. Let's try.

314
00:23:00,755 --> 00:23:02,841
Yeah.

315
00:23:02,924 --> 00:23:05,010
(whispers) ldiot.

316
00:23:09,014 --> 00:23:11,725
- (camera shutter clicks)
- Un, deux, trois,...

317
00:23:11,808 --> 00:23:12,767
..quatre.

318
00:23:12,851 --> 00:23:16,187
(Richard) When you develop
an infatuation for someone,...

319
00:23:16,271 --> 00:23:20,817
..you always find a reason to believe
that this is exactly the person foryou.

320
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:23,153
lt doesn't need to be a good reason.

321
00:23:23,236 --> 00:23:26,489
Taking photographs of the night sky,
for example.

322
00:23:26,573 --> 00:23:28,658
Now, in the long run,...

323
00:23:28,742 --> 00:23:33,621
..that's just the kind ofdumb, irritating habit
that would cause you to split up.

324
00:23:33,705 --> 00:23:35,957
But in the haze of infatuation,...

325
00:23:36,708 --> 00:23:40,587
..it's just what you've been searching for
all these years.

326
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:49,637
- (Étienne) One kilometre.
- (Francoise) Two.

327
00:23:49,721 --> 00:23:53,641
- (Étienne) Richard?
- l don't know. l'm American.

328
00:23:53,725 --> 00:23:56,936
- So?
- We think in miles, not kilometres.

329
00:23:57,020 --> 00:23:59,522
OK. So how many miles do you think it is?

330
00:24:00,607 --> 00:24:04,277
l don't know.
But it looks like a long way away.

331
00:24:04,361 --> 00:24:07,030
lf it's too far, we're gonna drown.

332
00:24:11,659 --> 00:24:14,162
But if we don't try,
we'll never know, right?

333
00:24:15,246 --> 00:24:16,998
Right.

334
00:24:21,044 --> 00:24:23,296
So let's go!

335
00:24:23,380 --> 00:24:26,257
(** "Beached" by Angelo Badalamenti)

336
00:24:30,929 --> 00:24:32,639
- (splash)
- Whoo!

337
00:24:57,664 --> 00:25:00,875
- Are you guys all right?
- (Étienne) Yeah, we're OK.

338
00:25:00,959 --> 00:25:03,044
l think we're about half way.

339
00:25:07,007 --> 00:25:09,759
Oh, fuck! Richard!

340
00:25:10,468 --> 00:25:12,554
- (Étienne) Fuck!
- What?

341
00:25:12,637 --> 00:25:14,389
l saw a fin!

342
00:25:14,472 --> 00:25:17,475
- Tsk! What? Are you joking?
- (Étienne) No, no, no!

343
00:25:17,559 --> 00:25:19,185
A fin!

344
00:25:20,228 --> 00:25:21,688
OK, a shark fin?

345
00:25:21,771 --> 00:25:25,734
l don't know. Just a fin.
Over there, about 100 metres.

346
00:25:28,028 --> 00:25:31,156
- Well, was it big?
- Yes.

347
00:25:33,158 --> 00:25:35,452
What the fuck do you expect me
to do about it?!

348
00:25:35,535 --> 00:25:38,121
Nothing! l just thought you should know.

349
00:25:38,204 --> 00:25:40,457
To be honest, l'd rather you hadn't told me!

350
00:25:40,540 --> 00:25:44,502
- OK, l'm sorry.
- Well, it's a bit fuckin' late now, isn't it?!

351
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:55,638
(Étienne screams)

352
00:25:55,722 --> 00:25:59,100
Francoise! Francoise! She's gone!

353
00:25:59,184 --> 00:26:00,810
Oh, my God!

354
00:26:00,894 --> 00:26:05,815
- Oh, my God! OK, what happened?
- (Étienne) She just went under the water!

355
00:26:05,899 --> 00:26:07,984
She was pulled under!

356
00:26:09,778 --> 00:26:11,279
(Étienne) Francoise!

357
00:26:11,363 --> 00:26:14,115
Francoise! l don't see her!

358
00:26:14,908 --> 00:26:16,826
Oh, fuck! lt's her bag!

359
00:26:16,910 --> 00:26:20,580
OK. Was there a shark?
Did you see a shark, Étienne?

360
00:26:20,663 --> 00:26:22,665
l don't know!

361
00:26:22,749 --> 00:26:24,501
l don't know!

362
00:26:24,584 --> 00:26:26,503
Fuck!

363
00:26:27,045 --> 00:26:28,213
Don't fuck me!

364
00:26:30,131 --> 00:26:31,549
(screams)

365
00:26:32,467 --> 00:26:35,303
- (Francoise screams)
- (Richard screams)

366
00:26:35,387 --> 00:26:37,597
(Richard) Fuck you!

367
00:26:37,681 --> 00:26:39,766
(hysterical gasps)

368
00:26:39,849 --> 00:26:41,851
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

369
00:26:41,935 --> 00:26:44,020
(Richard laughs hysterically)

370
00:26:44,104 --> 00:26:46,773
Oh, you Europeans, you're so funny(!)

371
00:26:46,856 --> 00:26:49,859
You have such a play ful sense of humour(!)

372
00:26:49,943 --> 00:26:53,113
No wonder your comedy
has conquered the world(!)

373
00:26:53,196 --> 00:26:55,907
- What about Moliére?
- Who?

374
00:26:56,449 --> 00:26:58,118
Oh, fuck off!

375
00:27:54,382 --> 00:27:56,092
- Agh!
- (Richard) Come on.

376
00:28:01,473 --> 00:28:02,557
(grunts)

377
00:28:11,399 --> 00:28:13,485
(Étienne) Wow!

378
00:28:15,945 --> 00:28:18,031
(Étienne laughs)

379
00:28:22,911 --> 00:28:26,122
Now, this is what l call a lot of dope!

380
00:28:26,206 --> 00:28:28,291
(chuckles)

381
00:28:31,294 --> 00:28:33,380
(Étienne) Oh, put ain!

382
00:28:39,636 --> 00:28:41,721
T'as dupapierá rouler?

383
00:28:41,805 --> 00:28:43,515
(chuckles)

384
00:28:45,934 --> 00:28:48,269
(monkey chatters)

385
00:28:50,730 --> 00:28:53,233
Hey! Tch, tch, tch!

386
00:29:11,418 --> 00:29:13,503
(monkey screeches)

387
00:29:16,756 --> 00:29:18,842
(screeching)

388
00:29:26,933 --> 00:29:29,102
(mutters)

389
00:29:40,405 --> 00:29:42,490
(shouts in Thai)

390
00:29:51,458 --> 00:29:52,959
(shouting in Thai)

391
00:29:59,591 --> 00:30:01,676
OK... OK...

392
00:30:02,427 --> 00:30:05,930
(whispers) We're gonna go this way.
OK? Shut up. Shut up.

393
00:30:12,395 --> 00:30:14,356
(speaks in Thai)

394
00:30:37,921 --> 00:30:39,881
(chatter in Thai)

395
00:30:47,639 --> 00:30:48,973
(mouths)

396
00:30:49,057 --> 00:30:50,725
(hisses)

397
00:31:33,893 --> 00:31:35,979
Argh! Agh!

398
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,286
Sure, we should've turned back.

399
00:31:52,078 --> 00:31:54,164
But l wasn'tgoing to.

400
00:31:54,247 --> 00:31:56,332
Not now.

401
00:31:56,416 --> 00:31:58,960
l just kept telling them we'd get there.

402
00:31:59,044 --> 00:32:00,628
"Trust me,...

403
00:32:00,712 --> 00:32:03,089
..it's paradise."

404
00:32:03,173 --> 00:32:06,343
lf we take this down,
it should lead us all the way.

405
00:32:07,927 --> 00:32:10,013
Come on!

406
00:32:42,921 --> 00:32:45,006
(Richard) Oh, God!

407
00:32:53,598 --> 00:32:56,518
Putain de merde!

408
00:33:02,273 --> 00:33:04,359
(Étienne) Well?

409
00:33:04,442 --> 00:33:08,071
- (Richard) Well what?
- (Étienne) How do we get down?

410
00:33:08,154 --> 00:33:11,658
How am l supposed to know?
Do l have to decide everything?

411
00:33:11,741 --> 00:33:14,869
- We'll jump.
- Fuck! You wanted to be in command!

412
00:33:14,953 --> 00:33:18,915
l only took command because
you lost your nerve, French boy!

413
00:33:18,998 --> 00:33:21,418
Yeah. And look where you've taken us!

414
00:33:22,711 --> 00:33:24,796
- We'll jump.
- lf you're not happy,...

415
00:33:24,879 --> 00:33:27,298
..you can just take over. All right, sir?!

416
00:33:27,382 --> 00:33:29,384
(Étienne) All right, l will.

417
00:33:29,467 --> 00:33:32,887
- There. We climb down there.
- We can jump.

418
00:33:32,971 --> 00:33:36,057
Francoise! Look... We're not gonnajump!

419
00:33:36,141 --> 00:33:39,269
All right? So just can it!
And as for climbing down there,...

420
00:33:39,352 --> 00:33:40,645
..that is just...

421
00:33:40,729 --> 00:33:43,523
..an asshole suggestion!

422
00:33:45,775 --> 00:33:50,030
- Calling me an asshole?
- Yeah. And that's just the start of it.

423
00:33:50,113 --> 00:33:52,907
- All right, fuck face, let's do it!
- Motherfucker!

424
00:33:53,616 --> 00:33:54,868
(Étienne) Francoise!

425
00:33:58,747 --> 00:34:01,583
- Shit!
- Francoise!

426
00:34:06,963 --> 00:34:09,341
Come on, guys! lt's OK!

427
00:34:09,424 --> 00:34:12,719
lt's not dangerous! Come on!

428
00:34:12,802 --> 00:34:15,263
Drop the bags down! Come on!

429
00:34:15,347 --> 00:34:18,266
All right. So we'll jump.

430
00:34:18,350 --> 00:34:20,894
Oh, fuck!

431
00:34:22,145 --> 00:34:24,731
(both yell)

432
00:34:31,196 --> 00:34:33,782
(screams) Whoa!

433
00:34:33,865 --> 00:34:35,867
Whoo-hoo!

434
00:34:35,950 --> 00:34:38,203
Did you see that? Shit!

435
00:34:38,286 --> 00:34:40,372
Whoo! Whoo-hoo!

436
00:34:40,455 --> 00:34:41,748
Yes!

437
00:34:41,831 --> 00:34:43,917
Whoo-hoo!

438
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:46,086
(jubilant laughter)

439
00:34:54,636 --> 00:34:57,305
(Richard) Oh, my God!

440
00:34:59,057 --> 00:35:01,976
Congratulations!

441
00:35:02,060 --> 00:35:05,814
Took me the best part of an hour
to work up the balls to do that.

442
00:35:07,899 --> 00:35:12,737
Mind you, l was on my own, so you have to
make allowances. Ya know what l mean?

443
00:35:14,239 --> 00:35:16,950
l think maybe you'd better meet up with Sal.

444
00:35:17,033 --> 00:35:19,953
Jesus Christ! We're fuckin' here!

445
00:35:20,036 --> 00:35:22,247
Do ya realise that?

446
00:35:25,875 --> 00:35:27,961
Don't you go anywhere!

447
00:35:34,592 --> 00:35:36,261
All right.

448
00:35:36,344 --> 00:35:38,430
You're doin' well.

449
00:35:39,347 --> 00:35:42,851
- Ciao! Sonja! A que sí?
- Hi.

450
00:35:48,606 --> 00:35:50,692
(man) Noisy kitchen!

451
00:35:50,775 --> 00:35:52,652
How are ya doin'?

452
00:35:52,736 --> 00:35:55,655
- What's for dinner?
- One guess. Fish.

453
00:35:55,739 --> 00:35:57,782
l don't know what we expected.

454
00:35:57,866 --> 00:36:01,494
People living in a cave,
maybe even a few guys in tents.

455
00:36:01,578 --> 00:36:02,829
Gregorio!

456
00:36:02,912 --> 00:36:04,914
But nothing like this.

457
00:36:04,998 --> 00:36:07,042
- How are you, Keaty?
- Don't smoke 'em!

458
00:36:07,125 --> 00:36:09,794
lt was like we arrived into a lost world.

459
00:36:09,878 --> 00:36:15,884
A full-scale community of travellers - not just
passing through, but actually living here.

460
00:36:19,637 --> 00:36:21,723
l suddenly became aware...

461
00:36:22,515 --> 00:36:24,601
..that we weren't even invited.

462
00:36:31,024 --> 00:36:33,693
- (Richard) The guy who drew it?
- Daffy.

463
00:36:34,361 --> 00:36:36,863
Yeah... Yeah. He's dead.

464
00:36:36,946 --> 00:36:39,157
(man) What? No way!

465
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:43,078
Yeah. He cut his wrists open
in a hotel room on the Khao San Road.

466
00:36:43,161 --> 00:36:46,289
- You have seen this?!
- Well, l came afterwards.

467
00:36:48,792 --> 00:36:51,711
Well, that's sad news.

468
00:36:52,671 --> 00:36:55,715
He was... one of the founders
of our community.

469
00:36:55,799 --> 00:36:57,425
Oh.

470
00:36:57,509 --> 00:36:59,594
But he became depressed.

471
00:36:59,678 --> 00:37:02,180
(woman) Crazy.

472
00:37:03,431 --> 00:37:08,436
The police didn't know what to do with
the body, so l guess they'll incinerate him.

473
00:37:13,108 --> 00:37:16,236
Do you think he gave a map to anybody else?

474
00:37:16,319 --> 00:37:18,571
l-l... No, l don't think so.

475
00:37:19,489 --> 00:37:22,200
And you. Have you
shown this map to anybody?

476
00:37:22,283 --> 00:37:23,326
No.

477
00:37:24,035 --> 00:37:25,078
No.

478
00:37:26,037 --> 00:37:27,580
No.

479
00:37:29,541 --> 00:37:30,792
Good.

480
00:37:33,128 --> 00:37:36,131
We value our secrecy.

481
00:37:36,214 --> 00:37:38,299
(murmurs of agreement)

482
00:37:40,260 --> 00:37:42,679
- (man) Yeah!
- (woman) Whoo!

483
00:37:45,932 --> 00:37:48,935
(** "Porcelain" by Moby)

484
00:37:58,236 --> 00:38:00,321
(chorus of animals)

485
00:38:01,031 --> 00:38:03,116
You hear that? You hear that?

486
00:38:04,409 --> 00:38:06,244
(imitates monkey)

487
00:38:06,327 --> 00:38:08,413
Look at this guy.

488
00:38:40,737 --> 00:38:42,822
(joyous laughter)

489
00:38:44,115 --> 00:38:46,284
Oh, c'est magnifique.

490
00:38:57,504 --> 00:38:59,589
(incredulous chuckling)

491
00:39:04,678 --> 00:39:07,013
Oh, it's so fucking beautiful, man!

492
00:39:39,629 --> 00:39:42,507
- Neighbours!
- Hey! l've got your oils, man.

493
00:39:44,843 --> 00:39:46,928
l want to give you something.

494
00:39:47,012 --> 00:39:50,598
- Listen up, everybody.
- (groaning)

495
00:39:50,682 --> 00:39:52,559
OK.

496
00:39:52,642 --> 00:39:56,229
Tomorrow, l will travel
for many miles on a bicycle.

497
00:39:57,230 --> 00:39:58,273
Um...

498
00:39:58,356 --> 00:39:59,399
Vicki.

499
00:39:59,482 --> 00:40:01,401
Uh... Uh...

500
00:40:01,484 --> 00:40:03,778
Uh... (Irish accent) Sutra cuputovati...

501
00:40:03,862 --> 00:40:05,822
..mnogo milja biciklom.

502
00:40:05,905 --> 00:40:08,366
Great! Very good. Héléne?

503
00:40:08,450 --> 00:40:10,535
Very good!

504
00:40:10,618 --> 00:40:15,373
(French accent)
Sutra cuputovati... mnogo milja biciklom.

505
00:40:15,457 --> 00:40:16,791
(woman) Very good.

506
00:40:17,834 --> 00:40:20,003
Right. lt's far too easy, though.

507
00:40:20,086 --> 00:40:23,256
- (woman) Oh, please!
- (Keaty) Yes! OK.

508
00:40:23,798 --> 00:40:27,886
Sutra cuputovati mnogo
milja biciklom. Da posetim svoju tatu...

509
00:40:27,969 --> 00:40:33,308
..koji èuva koze na planini.
There's more, ya know!

510
00:40:33,391 --> 00:40:36,561
- You always know everything!
- (Keaty) Richard!

511
00:40:37,729 --> 00:40:39,814
(clears throat)

512
00:40:39,898 --> 00:40:41,441
Sutra...

513
00:40:41,524 --> 00:40:43,068
..cu...

514
00:40:43,151 --> 00:40:44,611
..putovati...

515
00:40:44,694 --> 00:40:46,780
..mnogo milja biciklom.

516
00:40:46,863 --> 00:40:48,281
(Keaty) Yes! Richard!

517
00:40:48,365 --> 00:40:50,283
Represented, man!

518
00:40:50,367 --> 00:40:53,912
(man sings) Sutra cuputovati
mnogo milja biciklom.

519
00:40:54,913 --> 00:40:56,456
This became our world.

520
00:40:57,415 --> 00:40:59,751
And these people, our family.

521
00:41:01,294 --> 00:41:04,881
Back home was just one more place
we didn't think about.

522
00:41:05,423 --> 00:41:07,217
l settled in.

523
00:41:07,300 --> 00:41:09,177
l found my vocation:

524
00:41:09,260 --> 00:41:11,346
..the pursuit...

525
00:41:11,429 --> 00:41:13,014
..of pleasure.

526
00:41:13,098 --> 00:41:15,183
(** "Spinning Away" by Sugar Ray)

527
00:41:27,278 --> 00:41:29,364
Sal was the leader.

528
00:41:29,447 --> 00:41:33,576
But it wasn't a big deal. l mean,
there wasn't any ideology or shit like that.

529
00:41:33,660 --> 00:41:37,747
lt was just a beach resort...
for people who don't like beach resorts.

530
00:41:37,831 --> 00:41:39,416
..some of us build.

531
00:41:39,499 --> 00:41:42,585
Even paradise takes a little shaping.

532
00:41:46,798 --> 00:41:48,925
For years, they kept this place a secret.

533
00:41:49,009 --> 00:41:53,388
They didn't need to tell anyone.
They were practically self-sufficient.

534
00:41:53,471 --> 00:41:59,686
They just had to sail back once in a while
to trade a little marijuana and buy some rice.

535
00:42:02,063 --> 00:42:05,859
We grow our own, so no stealing
from the farmers on the other side.

536
00:42:05,942 --> 00:42:08,361
And do they know that you're living here?

537
00:42:08,445 --> 00:42:12,907
Oh, yeah. But they keep to their side
and we don't trespass on their turf.

538
00:42:12,991 --> 00:42:17,954
A couple of years ago, they said that we
could stay, but nobody else should come.

539
00:42:18,038 --> 00:42:21,166
- Which kind of suits us as well.
- So you was lucky, ya know.

540
00:42:21,249 --> 00:42:22,709
Very lucky.

541
00:42:22,792 --> 00:42:25,545
There was Keaty, who only cared
about two things.

542
00:42:25,628 --> 00:42:27,714
Thank you, Lord,...

543
00:42:27,797 --> 00:42:30,675
..for the twin pillars of civilisation:

544
00:42:31,634 --> 00:42:33,136
..Christianity...

545
00:42:33,219 --> 00:42:35,972
..and cricket.

546
00:42:39,267 --> 00:42:40,769
There were the Swedes:

547
00:42:40,852 --> 00:42:42,937
..Christo, Sten and Karl.

548
00:42:43,021 --> 00:42:45,106
We like fishing.

549
00:42:46,941 --> 00:42:49,652
- And in the winter, we like skiing.
- Yeah!

550
00:42:51,279 --> 00:42:53,948
Of course, in Thailand, there is no skiing.

551
00:42:54,032 --> 00:42:56,534
(Christo) We wait, OK?

552
00:42:56,618 --> 00:42:58,912
We wait for the fish to come.

553
00:43:03,458 --> 00:43:04,876
Get it?

554
00:43:04,959 --> 00:43:07,796
- Shit! No way!
- (Étienne) Whoo!

555
00:43:07,879 --> 00:43:11,091
And l said to thee "l shall provide!"

556
00:43:11,174 --> 00:43:12,884
Yeah!

557
00:43:16,221 --> 00:43:18,056
- Stop it.
- What?

558
00:43:23,019 --> 00:43:25,814
Our resident chef was known as Unhygenix.

559
00:43:25,897 --> 00:43:27,482
Let's cook!

560
00:43:27,565 --> 00:43:29,818
On account of his obsession with soap.

561
00:43:29,901 --> 00:43:31,986
Fish, fish, fish!

562
00:43:36,783 --> 00:43:38,868
Still l smell of fish!

563
00:43:38,952 --> 00:43:43,832
There was a range of sporting
and leisure activities to suit all tastes.

564
00:43:43,915 --> 00:43:46,001
Étienne is good at soccer.

565
00:43:46,084 --> 00:43:49,045
Ya know, l could do that if l wanted to.

566
00:43:49,129 --> 00:43:52,007
- l just don't want to.
- What are you talking about?

567
00:43:53,091 --> 00:43:56,511
- Making conversation.
- Do you have a girlfriend?

568
00:43:57,178 --> 00:43:59,264
- Here?
- Anywhere.

569
00:44:00,682 --> 00:44:03,143
No. Why?

570
00:44:03,935 --> 00:44:06,146
Just making conversation.

571
00:44:07,480 --> 00:44:09,566
- (cheering)
- Whoo!

572
00:44:12,110 --> 00:44:17,866
Right arm over wicket. Three balls remaining.
ls there anyone who still doesn't understand?

573
00:44:26,583 --> 00:44:31,755
The only person l didn't like was Sal's
boyfriend, Bugs - our on-island carpenter.

574
00:44:31,838 --> 00:44:33,923
Hey, Richard! Can you do this?

575
00:44:34,883 --> 00:44:37,010
Can you make anything?

576
00:44:38,845 --> 00:44:41,348
A man should have a talent in his hands.

577
00:44:42,557 --> 00:44:44,726
- Here we go, people!
- (whooping)

578
00:44:44,809 --> 00:44:46,603
Surprise!

579
00:44:46,686 --> 00:44:49,439
So every community has its rituals.

580
00:44:49,522 --> 00:44:53,902
Well, ours was simple:
the last one to arrive tattoos the next.

581
00:44:53,985 --> 00:44:56,071
lt fuckin' hurts, OK?

582
00:44:56,154 --> 00:44:58,740
What did he say? (screams)

583
00:44:58,823 --> 00:45:01,409
(laughter and cheering)

584
00:45:01,493 --> 00:45:02,577
Agh!

585
00:45:04,913 --> 00:45:07,290
Andy, bring yours closer.

586
00:45:07,374 --> 00:45:09,459
(Étienne) Come on, Richard!

587
00:45:14,673 --> 00:45:16,883
Ohhhh, God!

588
00:45:16,966 --> 00:45:18,593
(cheering)

589
00:45:18,677 --> 00:45:21,054
Ohh, God!

590
00:45:21,596 --> 00:45:23,682
Ohh, Jesus!

591
00:45:24,391 --> 00:45:27,519
(Richard) That fuckin' hurt!

592
00:45:27,602 --> 00:45:29,688
(cheering)

593
00:45:31,106 --> 00:45:34,067
All in all, this really was paradise.

594
00:45:34,150 --> 00:45:36,236
Except for one thing.

595
00:45:37,278 --> 00:45:39,364
Desire is desire,...

596
00:45:39,447 --> 00:45:41,408
..wherever you go.

597
00:45:41,491 --> 00:45:43,576
The sun will not bleach it,...

598
00:45:43,660 --> 00:45:46,162
..nor the tide wash it away.

599
00:45:47,789 --> 00:45:49,874
Francoise.

600
00:46:24,868 --> 00:46:26,911
One: she's just teasin' ya.

601
00:46:26,995 --> 00:46:29,497
(Richard) What are you talking about?

602
00:46:29,581 --> 00:46:31,624
Two: you don't speak French.

603
00:46:31,708 --> 00:46:33,793
Three: he speaks French.

604
00:46:33,877 --> 00:46:36,296
ln fact, even better than that, four:

605
00:46:36,379 --> 00:46:38,465
..he is French.

606
00:46:39,090 --> 00:46:43,678
Five: he's much better at football -
sorry, soccer - than you.

607
00:46:44,387 --> 00:46:47,057
And six: you're a bit strange, Rich.

608
00:46:47,140 --> 00:46:51,019
Some girls like that in a man, but not
the sort of girls you wanna be with.

609
00:46:51,102 --> 00:46:54,689
- ls that right?
- Come on, your last girlfriend chucked ya.

610
00:46:54,773 --> 00:46:58,026
- lt was not my fault!
- And seven: look at your thumbs, man!

611
00:46:58,109 --> 00:47:00,904
- They're well-defined.
- What does that mean?

612
00:47:00,987 --> 00:47:03,073
You play a lot of video games!

613
00:47:03,907 --> 00:47:06,868
That is a powerful index of incompatibility.

614
00:47:07,452 --> 00:47:10,830
Why do l get the feeling
you're trying to tell me something?

615
00:47:10,914 --> 00:47:14,417
You haven't a hope - not a bleedin'
chicken's chance in Thailand.

616
00:47:14,501 --> 00:47:16,920
- Know what l mean?
- Thank you.

617
00:47:17,754 --> 00:47:20,548
So, enjoy the beach and cut the bullshit.

618
00:47:20,632 --> 00:47:23,885
- (softly) Thank you very much.
- lt's my pleasure!

619
00:47:25,053 --> 00:47:27,138
(Gregorio) No, you cannot... No!

620
00:47:27,222 --> 00:47:29,683
No! No, leave me!

621
00:47:29,766 --> 00:47:31,768
- Leave me!
- (woman) Hey! That's my bed!

622
00:47:31,851 --> 00:47:34,854
- l can deal with it!
- l don't want you to deal with it!

623
00:47:34,938 --> 00:47:36,898
(Bugs) lt won't take a minute.

624
00:47:36,981 --> 00:47:39,901
Really, no! No, l must go to mainland!

625
00:47:40,652 --> 00:47:43,738
l'm sick. l've got to. Sal!

626
00:47:43,822 --> 00:47:47,492
What's this? You want to go
to the mainland to see a dentist?

627
00:47:47,575 --> 00:47:50,370
- Yes.
- lt's out of the question.

628
00:47:50,453 --> 00:47:52,414
(laughter)

629
00:47:52,497 --> 00:47:54,582
Come on!

630
00:47:54,666 --> 00:47:56,751
lt'll be fun.

631
00:47:56,835 --> 00:47:58,378
(woman) Be brave.

632
00:47:58,461 --> 00:48:00,547
(Sal) How's it going, Richard?

633
00:48:01,589 --> 00:48:03,341
Fine. Fine.

634
00:48:03,425 --> 00:48:05,885
- Are you OK with this?
- Yeah.

635
00:48:07,137 --> 00:48:09,472
l mean, we have a secret here, right?

636
00:48:09,556 --> 00:48:13,226
Sometimes people need to
take a little pain to keep it that way.

637
00:48:14,269 --> 00:48:15,895
Excellent.

638
00:48:15,979 --> 00:48:18,064
Excellent attitude.

639
00:48:18,148 --> 00:48:20,692
No problem.

640
00:48:20,775 --> 00:48:23,653
- (Gregorio screams)
- (Bugs) Oh, shit!

641
00:48:23,737 --> 00:48:25,655
(laughter)

642
00:48:27,365 --> 00:48:30,910
- Good work!
- (Gregorio sobs)

643
00:48:30,994 --> 00:48:33,872
- Kill the pain, boy.
- (Gregorio gasps)

644
00:48:35,707 --> 00:48:37,792
(jeering)

645
00:48:39,085 --> 00:48:41,421
Take a drink.

646
00:48:41,504 --> 00:48:43,590
(** "Pure Shores" by All Saints)

647
00:48:48,011 --> 00:48:50,096
(laughs weakly)

648
00:48:53,683 --> 00:48:55,769
(Francoise) Richard.

649
00:48:55,852 --> 00:48:57,228
Yeah?

650
00:48:57,312 --> 00:48:59,689
Would you like to come
to the beach with me?

651
00:49:05,612 --> 00:49:07,280
Sure. Yeah.

652
00:49:18,625 --> 00:49:20,710
Are you happy, Richard?

653
00:49:21,294 --> 00:49:23,213
Happy?

654
00:49:23,296 --> 00:49:24,422
Yeah.

655
00:49:24,506 --> 00:49:26,591
Yeah... Yeah, l-l guess.

656
00:49:26,675 --> 00:49:29,344
l mean, the beach, ya know, it's just perfect.

657
00:49:29,427 --> 00:49:31,513
Do you think that l ignore you?

658
00:49:35,058 --> 00:49:36,476
No.

659
00:49:36,559 --> 00:49:38,436
But l do.

660
00:49:38,520 --> 00:49:43,441
lt's because l'm with Étienne.
lt's difficult for me to spend time with you.

661
00:49:50,448 --> 00:49:55,036
l don't suppose that there's any...
you know, special reason that you should.

662
00:49:56,955 --> 00:49:59,958
- Spend time with me, that is.
- Of course there is.

663
00:50:00,041 --> 00:50:01,626
l like you.

664
00:50:01,710 --> 00:50:03,169
A lot.

665
00:50:03,253 --> 00:50:06,089
Have you... Have you
told this to Étienne? Or...

666
00:50:06,172 --> 00:50:07,215
No.

667
00:50:07,298 --> 00:50:09,592
lt's our secret.

668
00:50:10,635 --> 00:50:11,845
OK.

669
00:50:12,846 --> 00:50:16,016
Look! There! The plankton. Shrimps.

670
00:50:16,099 --> 00:50:18,226
When they're disturbed, they glow.

671
00:50:18,309 --> 00:50:20,395
Come on!

672
00:50:21,062 --> 00:50:25,442
** l'm coming, not drowning
Swimming closer to you

673
00:51:04,147 --> 00:51:05,857
** l'm moving

674
00:51:05,940 --> 00:51:08,026
** l feelit

675
00:51:09,402 --> 00:51:11,488
** l'm coming, not drowning

676
00:51:14,240 --> 00:51:16,326
** l'm moving, l feelit

677
00:51:18,703 --> 00:51:22,082
** l'm coming, not drowning

678
00:51:22,999 --> 00:51:25,085
** l'm moving, l'm coming

679
00:51:25,168 --> 00:51:27,253
** Can you hear what l hear?

680
00:51:27,337 --> 00:51:29,422
** lt's calling you, my dear...

681
00:51:29,506 --> 00:51:33,635
(Richard) That night, we promised ourselves,
and we honestly believed,...

682
00:51:33,718 --> 00:51:35,804
..that no one would everknow.

683
00:51:38,014 --> 00:51:40,809
- l wanna talk.
- About what?

684
00:51:41,476 --> 00:51:43,561
About you and Francoise.

685
00:51:43,645 --> 00:51:46,940
Whaddaya mean... me and Francoise?

686
00:51:49,776 --> 00:51:51,861
l mean, Richard,...

687
00:51:53,071 --> 00:51:55,448
- ..that l want her to be happy.
- Yeah.

688
00:51:55,532 --> 00:51:57,617
l mean, of course.

689
00:51:57,701 --> 00:51:59,994
- We all do, right?
- Shut up!

690
00:52:01,121 --> 00:52:03,289
Please shut the fuck up.

691
00:52:08,378 --> 00:52:10,463
And if happy is with you,...

692
00:52:10,547 --> 00:52:13,216
..then l will not stand in her way.

693
00:52:16,094 --> 00:52:18,179
Étienne, man, l...

694
00:52:18,263 --> 00:52:22,851
- l don't know what you're talking about.
- Fuck you, Richard! l know!

695
00:52:22,934 --> 00:52:24,936
OK? l know!

696
00:52:25,020 --> 00:52:27,063
Everybody knows!

697
00:52:35,196 --> 00:52:37,157
(thunderclap)

698
00:52:38,283 --> 00:52:40,994
(Christo) The problem is seeing the fish.

699
00:52:41,703 --> 00:52:44,164
With the heavy rain and the bad light,...

700
00:52:44,247 --> 00:52:46,958
..it's very difficult to catch them.

701
00:52:47,042 --> 00:52:49,544
lt can last for days.

702
00:52:50,253 --> 00:52:52,297
Sometimes...

703
00:52:52,380 --> 00:52:54,466
..we get really hungry.

704
00:53:02,515 --> 00:53:04,476
Gimme that.

705
00:53:06,936 --> 00:53:08,730
Richard!

706
00:53:33,463 --> 00:53:35,548
Richard! Richard!

707
00:53:36,216 --> 00:53:38,426
Come out!

708
00:53:39,719 --> 00:53:41,805
l can't hear you!

709
00:53:42,847 --> 00:53:44,933
(thunder)

710
00:53:46,893 --> 00:53:49,187
And you can't hear me.

711
00:53:50,772 --> 00:53:53,316
- Shark!
- Come!

712
00:54:15,380 --> 00:54:16,339
Shark!

713
00:54:22,470 --> 00:54:24,931
Ohh!

714
00:54:29,894 --> 00:54:32,605
- All right, all right.
- (cheering)

715
00:54:32,689 --> 00:54:34,774
All right, all right, all right!

716
00:54:36,276 --> 00:54:37,527
Shh!

717
00:54:39,029 --> 00:54:43,199
Now before l start, there's just
a couple of things you have to remember.

718
00:54:44,993 --> 00:54:47,328
Number one: you have to remain calm.

719
00:54:47,412 --> 00:54:49,497
Right?

720
00:54:50,623 --> 00:54:53,877
And number two: you have to show no fear.

721
00:54:53,960 --> 00:54:56,588
- Teach it, teach it.
- Because the sharks...

722
00:54:56,671 --> 00:54:59,632
You see, the sharks, they can sense that fear.

723
00:55:00,425 --> 00:55:02,927
Just as easily as they can sense blood.

724
00:55:04,346 --> 00:55:06,431
And so it went forme.

725
00:55:06,514 --> 00:55:08,600
Just as l knew it would.

726
00:55:08,683 --> 00:55:10,769
Just as nature had or dained.

727
00:55:10,852 --> 00:55:13,396
lts... jaw wide open.

728
00:55:14,439 --> 00:55:20,987
Row upon row of these razor-sharp teeth
glinting underwater like... jagged diamonds.

729
00:55:21,071 --> 00:55:25,325
lt's tail fin sweeping back and forth
as it surged in for the kill.

730
00:55:26,618 --> 00:55:28,078
l swear to God,...

731
00:55:28,161 --> 00:55:30,705
..my whole life
flashed before my eyes.

732
00:55:32,457 --> 00:55:34,125
Really.

733
00:55:34,209 --> 00:55:37,087
l had nothing left to offer
except for pure reflex.

734
00:55:37,170 --> 00:55:38,755
Pure reflex...

735
00:55:38,838 --> 00:55:42,926
..and mankind's basic drive for survival
that somehow...

736
00:55:43,009 --> 00:55:47,055
..shouts "No! l will not die today!"

737
00:55:47,138 --> 00:55:49,766
- Yes!
- Whoo!

738
00:55:51,643 --> 00:55:54,729
At that instant, l knew
it was either the shark or me.

739
00:55:54,813 --> 00:55:57,065
The shark knew it.

740
00:55:57,148 --> 00:55:59,234
l knew it.

741
00:56:00,694 --> 00:56:02,487
But jeez... God!

742
00:56:02,570 --> 00:56:07,158
lt's nothin' personal, right? lt's just
the way the world works. lt's nature.

743
00:56:10,078 --> 00:56:12,247
But... if l remember correctly,...

744
00:56:14,874 --> 00:56:17,377
..in that last glimmer of its eyes,...

745
00:56:19,879 --> 00:56:22,090
..there was a moment between us...

746
00:56:26,094 --> 00:56:28,513
..where it said "Hey, Richard, man."

747
00:56:29,723 --> 00:56:31,266
"Enjoy your dinner. "

748
00:56:31,349 --> 00:56:33,435
(whooping andlaughter)

749
00:56:34,269 --> 00:56:36,104
(cheering)

750
00:56:45,113 --> 00:56:48,658
Strange thing, killing a shark,
isn't it, Richard?

751
00:56:51,494 --> 00:56:53,580
lt's just a big fish, Bugs.

752
00:56:53,663 --> 00:56:55,665
Just a big fish?

753
00:56:55,749 --> 00:57:00,587
Yeah, maybe! Maybe when it's just a baby
and it hasn't really learned to kill yet.

754
00:57:00,670 --> 00:57:02,756
Then maybe it's just a big fish.

755
00:57:03,548 --> 00:57:07,886
But when it's a great white angry mother
with the taste of blood on its tongue,...

756
00:57:07,969 --> 00:57:10,138
..now that's a different story.

757
00:57:18,438 --> 00:57:20,607
Oh, God! Jeez... (chuckles)

758
00:57:20,690 --> 00:57:22,776
l'm sorry, Bugs. ls it just me?

759
00:57:22,859 --> 00:57:25,695
Or does this wet weather
make everyone so damn tired?

760
00:57:25,779 --> 00:57:30,033
Maybe we can hear your very different
and, l'm sure, very interesting story...

761
00:57:30,116 --> 00:57:33,036
- ..some other time, huh?
- (exaggerated yawning)

762
00:57:35,789 --> 00:57:38,041
Very interesting, Keaty!

763
00:57:38,124 --> 00:57:41,044
Vrlo interesant no.

764
00:57:45,715 --> 00:57:48,635
Molto interessante!

765
00:57:48,718 --> 00:57:52,180
- Good night, young lovers.
- (chuckles) Shut up!

766
00:57:52,263 --> 00:57:56,101
For a while, we were untouchable
in our happiness.

767
00:57:59,979 --> 00:58:02,065
All right! Everybody!

768
00:58:02,148 --> 00:58:05,151
- (chatter continues)
