Or get better,...

1020
01:15:19,853 --> 01:15:22,355
..in which case everyone can forget about it.

1021
01:15:22,439 --> 01:15:25,984
- (man) l can't take this.
- (woman) Christo, please!

1022
01:15:26,067 --> 01:15:30,572
- (Christo cries out)
- "..every two or three autumns."

1023
01:15:30,655 --> 01:15:33,074
(woman) Great atmosphere(!)

1024
01:15:34,284 --> 01:15:37,287
- Get better or die.
- (Christo moans)

1025
01:15:37,370 --> 01:15:41,041
lt's the hanging around in between
that really pisses people off.

1026
01:15:41,124 --> 01:15:44,252
Listen to me. You can't do this.

1027
01:15:44,336 --> 01:15:46,421
This is disgusting!

1028
01:15:46,504 --> 01:15:48,506
Take him back!

1029
01:15:48,590 --> 01:15:51,885
- OK, just here.
- Fucking animals!

1030
01:15:54,304 --> 01:15:56,890
What are you doing this for? Huh?

1031
01:15:56,973 --> 01:15:59,142
Tell me!

1032
01:15:59,225 --> 01:16:01,436
How can you do this?

1033
01:16:06,649 --> 01:16:08,735
Richard!

1034
01:16:11,029 --> 01:16:13,114
Fucking bastards!

1035
01:16:14,949 --> 01:16:16,868
Bastards!

1036
01:16:16,951 --> 01:16:22,082
lt would be a lot easier to condemn
our behaviour if it hadn't been so effective.

1037
01:16:22,165 --> 01:16:24,209
But out of sight...

1038
01:16:24,292 --> 01:16:26,378
..really was out of mind.

1039
01:16:26,461 --> 01:16:28,546
Once he was gone,...

1040
01:16:28,630 --> 01:16:30,715
..we felt a whole lot better.

1041
01:16:32,133 --> 01:16:35,303
On the beach, it's easy to turn yourback,...

1042
01:16:35,387 --> 01:16:37,889
..but not always so easy to forget.

1043
01:17:18,972 --> 01:17:24,144
Pay them in dollars, fuck their daughters,
and turn it into Wonderland, Richard!

1044
01:17:26,312 --> 01:17:28,732
(whispers) Richard. Come with me.

1045
01:17:40,577 --> 01:17:43,413
(Sal) ls that, or is that not,...

1046
01:17:44,622 --> 01:17:46,708
..a map she's holding?

1047
01:17:48,501 --> 01:17:50,003
And did you,...

1048
01:17:50,086 --> 01:17:52,172
..or did you not,...

1049
01:17:53,214 --> 01:17:54,799
..make that copy?

1050
01:17:56,926 --> 01:17:59,804
You know, the lying doesn't bother me.

1051
01:18:00,638 --> 01:18:02,515
But that map...

1052
01:18:02,599 --> 01:18:04,100
..is trouble!

1053
01:18:04,184 --> 01:18:07,937
The farmers, right? You remember,
those men with guns?

1054
01:18:08,021 --> 01:18:10,106
They said to us, they told us...

1055
01:18:10,190 --> 01:18:12,067
.."No more people."

1056
01:18:12,150 --> 01:18:16,029
And now it looks like we're
handing out fucking tour guides!

1057
01:18:18,031 --> 01:18:20,116
Sal. l mean...

1058
01:18:21,117 --> 01:18:24,746
We could explain, right?
l mean, we could tell 'em it was Daffy.

1059
01:18:25,663 --> 01:18:27,749
We could explain?!

1060
01:18:31,878 --> 01:18:35,006
l want you up here every day
until those people come.

1061
01:18:35,090 --> 01:18:37,550
- Here?
- Yes, here.

1062
01:18:37,634 --> 01:18:39,678
l want you to get the map back.

1063
01:18:39,761 --> 01:18:42,389
OK? Whatever happens,
you get the map back.

1064
01:18:42,472 --> 01:18:43,848
W-Wait! Sal!

1065
01:18:43,932 --> 01:18:46,851
- Sal, they could be there for weeks!
- That's right.

1066
01:18:46,935 --> 01:18:51,272
- And you'll be here, waiting for them.
- What am l supposed to do when they come?

1067
01:18:51,356 --> 01:18:52,982
Get the map!!

1068
01:18:53,066 --> 01:18:57,487
You drew it! You handed it out!
Now you get it back and turn them away!

1069
01:18:59,823 --> 01:19:02,242
Sal! Sal!

1070
01:19:05,245 --> 01:19:07,872
Are you gonna tell 'em what else l did?

1071
01:19:15,922 --> 01:19:18,550
Now this was truly a pain in the ass.

1072
01:19:18,633 --> 01:19:22,262
l didn't want these people
to come here anymore than Sal did.

1073
01:19:22,345 --> 01:19:24,889
But what exactly did she expectme to do?

1074
01:19:24,973 --> 01:19:28,101
Chase them away? Threaten them?
l mean, with what?

1075
01:19:28,184 --> 01:19:32,313
By the time these kids gothere,
l'd probably have starved to death.

1076
01:19:32,397 --> 01:19:33,648
(movement)

1077
01:19:34,524 --> 01:19:35,775
Sal?

1078
01:19:35,859 --> 01:19:39,112
- Sal, is that you? Get that light outta...
- You're a pig!

1079
01:19:39,195 --> 01:19:42,449
Dammit! What the fuck was that for?
There's nothing l can do!

1080
01:19:42,532 --> 01:19:45,452
- l have to stay up here!
- Not that, OK?

1081
01:19:46,327 --> 01:19:49,289
- What is it, then?
- You and Sal in Ko Pha-Ngan.

1082
01:19:52,125 --> 01:19:53,376
Oh, that.

1083
01:19:53,460 --> 01:19:56,212
Yeah, that! She has told everyone!

1084
01:19:56,296 --> 01:19:58,381
And me, l'm the last one to find out!

1085
01:19:58,465 --> 01:20:01,217
At least she believes in honesty. Not like you.

1086
01:20:05,055 --> 01:20:07,140
l mean, Francoise, l...

1087
01:20:07,223 --> 01:20:09,351
What... what can l say?

1088
01:20:10,310 --> 01:20:12,812
Nothing. There's nothing you can say.

1089
01:20:18,443 --> 01:20:20,153
Thank you(!)

1090
01:20:20,236 --> 01:20:23,114
Thank you for making my life just perfect(!)

1091
01:20:25,075 --> 01:20:26,659
Super(!)

1092
01:20:27,202 --> 01:20:29,287
God...

1093
01:20:29,371 --> 01:20:31,456
..dammit!

1094
01:20:31,956 --> 01:20:34,042
Shit!

1095
01:20:35,460 --> 01:20:37,545
You are such an idiot!

1096
01:20:41,216 --> 01:20:44,844
Even though l knew it would happen...
l was crushed.

1097
01:20:45,762 --> 01:20:47,847
And l guess l deserved it.

1098
01:20:47,931 --> 01:20:51,059
l could a given her
all the excuses she wanted,...

1099
01:20:51,142 --> 01:20:53,603
..but it wouldn't have made any difference.

1100
01:20:54,354 --> 01:20:56,439
Great(!) Great(!)

1101
01:20:59,109 --> 01:21:02,070
At first, l thought l was gonna die up here,...

1102
01:21:02,153 --> 01:21:04,572
..that my entire world was gonna end.

1103
01:21:10,203 --> 01:21:12,288
But it didn't.

1104
01:21:22,841 --> 01:21:28,304
ln fact... pretty soon, l found that there were
plenty ofother things to keep me occupied.

1105
01:21:29,222 --> 01:21:31,307
And before l knew it,...

1106
01:21:31,391 --> 01:21:34,102
..l found that love, like grief,...

1107
01:21:34,769 --> 01:21:36,855
..tends to fade away...

1108
01:21:36,938 --> 01:21:39,983
..and be replaced by something more exciting.

1109
01:21:45,405 --> 01:21:48,908
And life up on the hill turned out
to be a big improvement.

1110
01:21:48,992 --> 01:21:51,494
l mean, up here, l could do whatever l wanted.

1111
01:21:51,578 --> 01:21:57,417
There was no fishing duty, no gardening shit,
no hassle from Bugs or Étienne or Francoise.

1112
01:21:57,500 --> 01:21:59,586
l was playing my own game now.

1113
01:22:00,378 --> 01:22:03,048
And l had absolutely no reason to go back.

1114
01:22:03,131 --> 01:22:05,800
(** "On Your Own:
Crouch End Broadway Mix" by Blur)

1115
01:22:50,303 --> 01:22:52,555
OK, so l was just foolin' around.

1116
01:22:55,433 --> 01:23:00,397
But the longer l stayed away from
the community,... the less l missed them.

1117
01:23:11,700 --> 01:23:13,785
And l found new players.

1118
01:23:15,120 --> 01:23:17,455
Even if they didn't know it yet.

1119
01:24:09,549 --> 01:24:11,634
This forest was my territory.

1120
01:24:16,222 --> 01:24:18,808
Retrieving the map,... mymission.

1121
01:24:22,979 --> 01:24:25,065
And these,...

1122
01:24:25,148 --> 01:24:27,233
..my defenders.

1123
01:24:29,986 --> 01:24:32,489
l was the only one with the overview...

1124
01:24:33,698 --> 01:24:36,618
..of how it all fitted together.

1125
01:24:39,162 --> 01:24:41,247
The island.

1126
01:24:43,249 --> 01:24:45,335
Me.

1127
01:24:46,753 --> 01:24:48,838
Them.

1128
01:24:50,632 --> 01:24:52,717
The invaders.

1129
01:24:59,224 --> 01:25:01,893
All connected.

1130
01:25:02,727 --> 01:25:04,813
All playing the same game.

1131
01:25:04,896 --> 01:25:06,981
(birds chatter)

1132
01:25:09,150 --> 01:25:11,236
And at the centre of it all,...

1133
01:25:11,319 --> 01:25:12,862
..one man:

1134
01:25:17,242 --> 01:25:18,535
..Daffy.

1135
01:25:21,204 --> 01:25:23,623
(helicopter)

1136
01:25:37,929 --> 01:25:40,015
lnside!

1137
01:25:43,643 --> 01:25:46,479
Take a look, Richard!

1138
01:25:46,563 --> 01:25:48,356
Viruses, Richard!

1139
01:25:48,440 --> 01:25:49,816
Cancers!

1140
01:25:49,899 --> 01:25:54,029
The big, chunky Charlie's
eating up the whole world! Out there!

1141
01:25:55,447 --> 01:25:58,867
Down on the beach! Down on
the street! Pay them in dollars...

1142
01:25:58,950 --> 01:26:02,203
..and fuck their daughters!

1143
01:26:03,246 --> 01:26:04,956
lt starts with four!

1144
01:26:05,040 --> 01:26:07,667
Four! But they multiply! They multiply!

1145
01:26:07,751 --> 01:26:10,211
lt's time to stop them!

1146
01:26:13,131 --> 01:26:14,758
Year zero, kiddo!

1147
01:26:16,384 --> 01:26:18,470
Year zero!

1148
01:26:18,928 --> 01:26:21,014
Are you with me or against me?

1149
01:26:21,514 --> 01:26:23,600
l'm with ya all the way, Daffy!

1150
01:26:26,144 --> 01:26:29,898
Ye-ea-ah! Yeah! Yeah!

1151
01:26:38,990 --> 01:26:41,076
(door opens)

1152
01:26:45,872 --> 01:26:47,332
Richard?

1153
01:26:47,415 --> 01:26:48,750
Yeah...

1154
01:26:48,833 --> 01:26:50,919
Where you been, man?!

1155
01:26:52,712 --> 01:26:55,256
What are you doing, sitting in the dark?

1156
01:26:55,924 --> 01:26:58,218
lmproving my night vision.

1157
01:26:58,301 --> 01:27:00,387
What for, mate?

1158
01:27:01,554 --> 01:27:03,640
You know who l think about a lot?

1159
01:27:05,475 --> 01:27:07,560
l have no idea.

1160
01:27:11,648 --> 01:27:13,191
Daffy.

1161
01:27:14,150 --> 01:27:15,985
Daffy?

1162
01:27:16,069 --> 01:27:17,529
Uh-huh.

1163
01:27:21,533 --> 01:27:23,618
l admire him.

1164
01:27:24,744 --> 01:27:27,163
You hardly knew him.

1165
01:27:27,914 --> 01:27:30,000
True...

1166
01:27:31,710 --> 01:27:33,795
But he had a certain style.

1167
01:27:39,467 --> 01:27:42,095
- Come here!
- (grunts)

1168
01:27:42,178 --> 01:27:44,180
Fucking come here!

1169
01:27:44,764 --> 01:27:47,600
Yes! They're talking about you.

1170
01:27:52,063 --> 01:27:56,026
- (Bugs) You're moaning, that's all.
- (Gregorio) l'm not moaning.

1171
01:27:56,109 --> 01:28:00,280
- l need to find out what his problem is.
- (Bugs) Do you think l like the guy?

1172
01:28:00,363 --> 01:28:04,409
- (woman) What does he do all day?
- (Gregorio) He does no work in garden.

1173
01:28:04,492 --> 01:28:07,078
But he steals our food. l'm sure of it.

1174
01:28:07,162 --> 01:28:09,039
You hear what they're saying?

1175
01:28:09,122 --> 01:28:12,042
ldle, sponging, useless prick!

1176
01:28:13,043 --> 01:28:15,628
(Keaty) Now, get your fucking act together.

1177
01:28:15,712 --> 01:28:18,840
You can't run around in the dark
not talking to nobody.

1178
01:28:18,923 --> 01:28:22,552
What do you think you're playing at, man?
What's happened to you?

1179
01:28:22,635 --> 01:28:25,847
You was all right.
Just a couple of weeks ago, you was fine.

1180
01:28:25,930 --> 01:28:27,849
And now, what the fuck is going on?

1181
01:28:27,932 --> 01:28:30,018
Look at you!

1182
01:28:30,101 --> 01:28:32,187
And you're talking about Daffy?!

1183
01:28:32,270 --> 01:28:36,149
Daffy was a nutter, right?
He went out there and he lost it. He's gone!

1184
01:28:36,232 --> 01:28:38,318
Richard!

1185
01:28:38,860 --> 01:28:40,945
Richard!

1186
01:28:41,029 --> 01:28:43,156
Do you hear what l'm saying to you?

1187
01:28:44,157 --> 01:28:46,868
Don't lose it like him. Do ya understand?

1188
01:28:46,951 --> 01:28:49,662
Don't go there! Stay with us.
Come back, Rich!

1189
01:28:49,746 --> 01:28:53,249
These are good people.
They don't talk about people all the time.

1190
01:28:53,333 --> 01:28:56,670
They're talking about you
because you're fucked up!

1191
01:28:59,047 --> 01:29:01,549
(echoing whispers)

1192
01:29:03,510 --> 01:29:05,595
..too much sensation.

1193
01:29:11,559 --> 01:29:13,645
..got outta control.

1194
01:29:21,236 --> 01:29:25,824
(Sal's voice echoes) And now it looks like
we're handing out fucking tourguides!

1195
01:29:43,425 --> 01:29:45,510
Mushroom, Richard?

1196
01:29:47,595 --> 01:29:49,681
No, thank you, Daffy.

1197
01:29:50,390 --> 01:29:53,518
l don't need any help
to see the writing on the wall.

1198
01:29:53,601 --> 01:29:57,188
- l'm very glad to hear that, Richard.
- Gotta keep my head clear.

1199
01:29:57,272 --> 01:29:59,858
- Getting closer, any day now.
- Year zero?

1200
01:29:59,941 --> 01:30:02,027
That's the spirit, kiddo.

1201
01:30:03,111 --> 01:30:05,196
You know somethin'?

1202
01:30:05,780 --> 01:30:07,866
You led the way, Daffy.

1203
01:30:08,950 --> 01:30:11,369
You showed me the truth.

1204
01:30:14,330 --> 01:30:18,293
But it doesn't matter what lthink
any more. lt's up to you now.

1205
01:30:19,252 --> 01:30:21,254
l won't let you down.

1206
01:30:21,338 --> 01:30:23,131
Hey, Richard.

1207
01:30:23,214 --> 01:30:25,300
No offence but, erm...

1208
01:30:25,383 --> 01:30:27,552
..you're fucked in the head, man.

1209
01:30:30,305 --> 01:30:32,390
(helicopter)

1210
01:30:35,393 --> 01:30:38,563
lt's been really nice knowing you, Daffy.

1211
01:30:41,691 --> 01:30:43,777
(echoing whispers)

1212
01:30:49,908 --> 01:30:53,870
(Richard) We're on patrolin the Delta.
Search and destroy.

1213
01:30:53,953 --> 01:30:55,497
(echoing whispers)

1214
01:30:55,580 --> 01:30:57,665
We're not making any contact.

1215
01:30:57,749 --> 01:31:00,168
(echoing whispers continue)

1216
01:31:06,007 --> 01:31:10,845
- This lieutenant, he says to me...
- (lieutenant) Get out there and draw their fire!

1217
01:31:10,929 --> 01:31:16,267
- (Richard) lt's nevergonna happen, sir.
- (lieutenant) Are you refusing an order, son?

1218
01:31:16,351 --> 01:31:21,356
- (Richard) lt looks that way, sir.
- (lieutenant) "lt looks that way, sir"?!

1219
01:31:21,439 --> 01:31:23,024
(echoing giggles)

1220
01:31:23,108 --> 01:31:25,985
(Richard) Then my M-16 just went off, man.

1221
01:31:26,069 --> 01:31:28,488
lt just went off!

1222
01:31:28,571 --> 01:31:30,657
(echoes) lt just went off.

1223
01:31:31,366 --> 01:31:34,494
(shouts and echoing whispers overlap)

1224
01:33:40,328 --> 01:33:42,414
Let's go!

1225
01:33:42,497 --> 01:33:44,666
(Zeph) Come back, Sam!

1226
01:33:44,749 --> 01:33:46,543
(whooping)

1227
01:34:03,768 --> 01:34:06,688
There's no other explanation!
We're in dope heaven!

1228
01:34:11,443 --> 01:34:14,904
** l smoke two joints in the morning,
l smoke two joints at night

1229
01:34:14,988 --> 01:34:19,034
** l smoke two joints in the afternoon
and then l feel all right

1230
01:34:19,117 --> 01:34:21,453
** l smoke two joints in time of peace

1231
01:34:21,536 --> 01:34:23,121
** And two in time of war

1232
01:34:23,204 --> 01:34:27,125
** l smoke two joints before two joints
and then l smoke some more!

1233
01:34:27,208 --> 01:34:29,294
(Sammy chuckles)

1234
01:34:41,097 --> 01:34:43,350
- Hi.
- Oh, shit!

1235
01:34:44,476 --> 01:34:46,561
(Zeph) We're Americans.

1236
01:34:48,063 --> 01:34:49,481
Tourists.

1237
01:34:49,564 --> 01:34:52,817
- American.
- We, uh... we... we had a... a map.

1238
01:34:52,901 --> 01:34:55,653
And we... we came here,...

1239
01:34:55,737 --> 01:35:00,950
..but we made a mistake. We made a mistake.
And... and we're sorry. We'll go now.

1240
01:35:01,034 --> 01:35:03,286
(speaks Thai)

1241
01:35:03,370 --> 01:35:05,288
(speaks Thai)

1242
01:35:07,040 --> 01:35:09,167
- Come on...
- (Zeph) We go now.

1243
01:35:14,422 --> 01:35:16,508
- (nervous gasp)
- (Zeph) Um...

1244
01:35:16,591 --> 01:35:19,511
- We... we just wanna go.
- (Sammy) Give 'em somethin'.

1245
01:35:19,594 --> 01:35:21,680
- Give 'em some money.
- Well...

1246
01:35:21,763 --> 01:35:25,308
Look! American dollars.
l got American dollars. You want...

1247
01:35:25,392 --> 01:35:27,477
..American dol... money?

1248
01:35:27,560 --> 01:35:29,646
Here...

1249
01:35:30,522 --> 01:35:32,399
- You can have them!
- Hey, hey, hey!

1250
01:35:33,233 --> 01:35:34,859
Um...

1251
01:35:34,943 --> 01:35:38,029
- (mouths)
- l've... l've got my watch. lt plays a tune.

1252
01:35:39,531 --> 01:35:41,825
(girls scream hysterically)

1253
01:35:41,908 --> 01:35:45,537
(shouting in Thai)

1254
01:35:56,881 --> 01:35:58,133
(screams)

1255
01:36:00,176 --> 01:36:02,262
(screams) No! No!

1256
01:36:13,940 --> 01:36:16,443
- (hysterical gasps)
- (hisses)

1257
01:36:44,346 --> 01:36:45,722
(shouts in Thai)

1258
01:37:07,035 --> 01:37:09,120
(terrified gasps)

1259
01:37:30,433 --> 01:37:32,519
(screams)

1260
01:38:16,688 --> 01:38:19,149
(Sal) This is our sixth year!

1261
01:38:19,232 --> 01:38:21,317
(cheering and clapping)

1262
01:38:24,404 --> 01:38:26,489
l want to look ahead.

1263
01:38:27,824 --> 01:38:29,909
Because l see...

1264
01:38:29,993 --> 01:38:32,954
..that beyond any problems
that we might have had...

1265
01:38:33,038 --> 01:38:34,414
Right?

1266
01:38:34,497 --> 01:38:37,459
..beyond any problems that we might have,...

1267
01:38:39,419 --> 01:38:43,340
..that we have so much here to inspire us.

1268
01:38:44,382 --> 01:38:47,093
And l'm not just talking about the island.

1269
01:38:49,179 --> 01:38:51,264
l'm talking about you.

1270
01:38:52,724 --> 01:38:54,976
You are what makes this place work.

1271
01:38:57,187 --> 01:38:59,272
And it does.

1272
01:38:59,397 --> 01:39:01,274
(mutters of agreement)

1273
01:39:01,358 --> 01:39:04,652
(Richard) l tried to remember
the person l used to be.

1274
01:39:04,736 --> 01:39:06,821
But l just couldn't do it.

1275
01:39:06,905 --> 01:39:09,616
- To the island!
- (cheering and whooping)

1276
01:39:09,699 --> 01:39:11,326
To you!

1277
01:39:11,409 --> 01:39:13,495
And so long as l stayed here,...

1278
01:39:13,578 --> 01:39:15,663
And to the future!

1279
01:39:16,623 --> 01:39:18,708
..l'd never find him again.

1280
01:39:18,792 --> 01:39:21,044
(** "Yeke Yeke: Hard Floor Mix"
by Mory Kante)

1281
01:39:36,351 --> 01:39:40,146
Come with me! l've gotta talk to you!
Listen! l've got to talk to you!

1282
01:39:40,230 --> 01:39:41,856
- Stop!
- Mais ca ne va pas, ou quoi!

1283
01:39:41,940 --> 01:39:43,608
- Listen!
- Mais tu me laches?!

1284
01:39:43,692 --> 01:39:48,697
l've gotta talk to you! Stop!
Francoise, listen! l've gotta talk to you. Stop...

1285
01:39:48,780 --> 01:39:51,199
Dammit! Stop! Stop it!

1286
01:39:51,282 --> 01:39:53,576
Stop it! Stop it! Stop!

1287
01:39:53,660 --> 01:39:55,995
l'm not gonna hurt you! All right?

1288
01:39:56,079 --> 01:39:58,957
(panting) lt's just me. lt's just me - Richard.

1289
01:39:59,624 --> 01:40:01,418
Remember?

1290
01:40:01,501 --> 01:40:04,546
(panting) The guy... who can't play soccer?

1291
01:40:04,629 --> 01:40:06,756
The guy without a girlfriend?

1292
01:40:09,300 --> 01:40:11,052
l remember.

1293
01:40:12,137 --> 01:40:14,222
l've just been away for a while.

1294
01:40:15,015 --> 01:40:17,100
That's all.

1295
01:40:17,183 --> 01:40:19,269
That's all.

1296
01:40:20,228 --> 01:40:23,773
- lls ont tué quatre personnes.
- (Étienne) Le crois pas.

1297
01:40:23,857 --> 01:40:26,860
- ll est taré.
- Dis pas n'importe quoipour qu'on s'en aille!

1298
01:40:26,943 --> 01:40:29,696
- Tu crois quej'ai envie de resterici?!
- Listen!

1299
01:40:29,779 --> 01:40:34,451
Étienne, l've really fucked up! Four people
are dead. l don't know what else they'll do!

1300
01:40:34,534 --> 01:40:37,954
But we have to leave now!
That's it! Just the three of us.

1301
01:40:38,038 --> 01:40:40,957
- Just like before.
- Richard,...

1302
01:40:43,376 --> 01:40:45,462
..l can't leave him.

1303
01:40:46,421 --> 01:40:49,507
- Then we'll take him with us.
- But... look at him.

1304
01:40:49,591 --> 01:40:50,884
Look at him.

1305
01:40:50,967 --> 01:40:53,053
We can't move him.

1306
01:40:53,136 --> 01:40:55,221
lt's gangrene.

1307
01:40:55,305 --> 01:40:57,349
lt's spreading.

1308
01:40:57,432 --> 01:40:58,933
He's gonna die.

1309
01:40:59,017 --> 01:41:01,811
(** "Yeke Yeke: Hard Floor Mix"
by Mory Kante)

1310
01:41:09,527 --> 01:41:11,613
(Richard) Wait for me at the boat.

1311
01:41:25,627 --> 01:41:27,754
(softly) Viens, mon ange. On y va.

1312
01:41:36,346 --> 01:41:38,431
(speaks Thai)

1313
01:41:57,367 --> 01:42:01,871
Christo had suffered because
we wouldn't let anything spoil our fun.

1314
01:42:04,457 --> 01:42:06,543
ln the perfect beach resort,...

1315
01:42:06,626 --> 01:42:10,505
..nothing is allowed to interrupt
the pursuit of pleasure.

1316
01:42:11,673 --> 01:42:13,758
Not even dying.

1317
01:42:14,509 --> 01:42:16,594
(muffled moans)

1318
01:43:14,319 --> 01:43:15,987
(scream)

1319
